From: electric-firebird
Subject: [PATCH] Under Emscripten, count committed metadata changes for the bridge (Firebird 5.0)

Firebird 5.0 (v5.0-release) counterpart of
0007-count-metadata-commits-for-bridge.patch.  Firebird 5.0 predates
CacheVector (MetadataCache) and instead calls
DsqlStatementCache::purgeAllAttachments(tdbb) from DFW_perform_work() whenever
a transaction with deferred metadata work (TRA_deferred_meta) commits.

Because Firebird 5.0's Jrd::Statement holds existence references on relations
and routines (rel_use_count / Routine::addRef) that would cause delete_relation
or modify_procedure in DFW_perform_work to fail with isc_obj_in_use if an idle
statement in the WASM bridge cache still referenced the object,
purgeAllAttachments also invokes fb_wasm_purge_cached_statements() inside an
EngineCheckout before DFW_perform_work checks object use counts.

diff --git a/src/dsql/DsqlStatementCache.cpp b/src/dsql/DsqlStatementCache.cpp
index 9f8a6e2..6a3d4e1 100644
--- a/src/dsql/DsqlStatementCache.cpp
+++ b/src/dsql/DsqlStatementCache.cpp
@@ -28,9 +28,16 @@
 #include "../jrd/lck.h"
 #include "../jrd/lck_proto.h"
 
+#ifdef __EMSCRIPTEN__
+#include <atomic>
+#include "../jrd/jrd.h"
+std::atomic<unsigned long long> fb_wasm_metadata_commits{0};
+extern "C" void fb_wasm_purge_cached_statements();
+#endif
+
 using namespace Firebird;
 using namespace Jrd;
 
 
 // Class DsqlStatementCache
 
@@ -241,6 +248,13 @@ void DsqlStatementCache::purge(thread_db* tdbb, bool releaseLock)
 
 void DsqlStatementCache::purgeAllAttachments(thread_db* tdbb)
 {
+#ifdef __EMSCRIPTEN__
+	++fb_wasm_metadata_commits;
+	{
+		EngineCheckout cout(tdbb, FB_FUNCTION);
+		fb_wasm_purge_cached_statements();
+	}
+#endif
 	purge(tdbb, false);
 
 	fb_assert(!lock || lock->lck_logical == LCK_SR);
